<model version="NetLogo 7.0.4" snapToGrid="true">
  <code><![CDATA[__includes ["thermostat.nls"]]]></code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="10" wrappingAllowedX="false" y="10" frameRate="30.0" minPycor="-20" height="408" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="4.0" fontSize="11" wrappingAllowedY="false" width="24" tickCounterLabel="ticks" maxPycor="80" updateMode="1" maxPxcor="4" minPxcor="0"></view>
    <note x="40" y="10" backgroundDark="0" fontSize="11" width="115" markdown="true" height="58" textColorDark="-1" textColorLight="-16777216" backgroundLight="0">Orange = temperature&lt;br&gt;
Green = target&lt;br&gt;
Blue = ambient</note>

    <button x="170" y="10" height="40" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="90" display="Setup">setup</button>
    <button x="265" y="10" height="40" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="90" display="Step">step-once</button>
    <button x="360" y="10" height="40" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="true" kind="Observer" width="90" display="Go">go</button>
    <chooser x="170" y="58" height="55" variable="arm" current="1" width="280" display="arm"><choice type="string" value="passive"></choice><choice type="string" value="feedback"></choice></chooser>
    <slider x="170" step="1" y="118" max="60" width="280" display="initial-temperature" height="42" min="-10" direction="Horizontal" default="20" variable="initial-temperature"></slider>
    <slider x="170" step="1" y="163" max="60" width="280" display="ambient-temperature" height="42" min="-10" direction="Horizontal" default="20" variable="ambient-temperature"></slider>
    <slider x="170" step="1" y="208" max="60" width="280" display="setpoint" height="42" min="-10" direction="Horizontal" default="20" variable="setpoint"></slider>
    <slider x="170" step="0.01" y="253" max="0.5" width="280" display="relaxation-rate" height="42" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="0.05" variable="relaxation-rate"></slider>
    <slider x="170" step="0.05" y="298" max="2" width="280" display="controller-gain" height="42" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="0.25" variable="controller-gain"></slider>
    <slider x="170" step="0.5" y="343" max="20" width="280" display="max-control" height="42" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="2" variable="max-control"></slider>
    <slider x="170" step="10" y="388" max="500" width="280" display="max-ticks" height="42" min="10" direction="Horizontal" default="160" variable="max-ticks"></slider>

    <button x="10" y="435" height="38" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="140" display="Displace state">displace-state</button>
    <slider x="155" step="1" y="430" max="30" width="295" display="displacement-amount" height="45" min="-30" direction="Horizontal" default="15" variable="displacement-amount"></slider>
    <button x="10" y="480" height="38" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="140" display="Apply load">apply-load</button>
    <button x="10" y="522" height="38" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="140" display="Remove load">remove-load</button>
    <slider x="155" step="0.25" y="482" max="10" width="295" display="load-magnitude" height="45" min="-10" direction="Horizontal" default="-1.5" variable="load-magnitude"></slider>
    <button x="155" y="530" height="38" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="142" display="Block sensor">block-sensor</button>
    <button x="302" y="530" height="38" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="148" display="Restore sensor">restore-sensor</button>
    <button x="155" y="572" height="38" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="142" display="Disable actuator">disable-actuator</button>
    <button x="302" y="572" height="38" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="148" display="Restore actuator">restore-actuator</button>
    <button x="10" y="572" height="38" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="140" display="Clear all faults">clear-interventions</button>
    <button x="10" y="616" height="38" disableUntilTicks="true" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="440" display="Export trajectory CSV">export-trajectory "thermostat-trajectory.csv"</button>

    <monitor x="480" precision="3" y="10" height="52" fontSize="11" width="120" display="temperature">temperature</monitor>
    <monitor x="605" precision="3" y="10" height="52" fontSize="11" width="120" display="error">control-error</monitor>
    <monitor x="730" precision="3" y="10" height="52" fontSize="11" width="120" display="applied control">applied-control</monitor>
    <monitor x="855" precision="3" y="10" height="52" fontSize="11" width="120" display="external load">external-load</monitor>
    <monitor x="980" precision="0" y="10" height="52" fontSize="11" width="145" display="last intervention">last-event</monitor>

    <plot x="480" autoPlotX="true" yMax="50.0" autoPlotY="true" yAxis="temperature" y="72" xMin="0.0" height="270" legend="true" xMax="160.0" yMin="0.0" width="645" xAxis="tick" display="State and target">
      <setup>clear-plot</setup><update></update>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="temperature" color="-955883" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot temperature</update></pen>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="setpoint" color="-10899396" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot setpoint</update></pen>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="sensed" color="-13345367" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot sensed-temperature</update></pen>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="ambient" color="-13791810" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot ambient-temperature</update></pen>
    </plot>
    <plot x="480" autoPlotX="true" yMax="5.0" autoPlotY="true" yAxis="term per tick" y="350" xMin="0.0" height="270" legend="true" xMax="160.0" yMin="-5.0" width="645" xAxis="tick" display="Dynamics">
      <setup>clear-plot</setup><update></update>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="commanded" color="-2674135" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot commanded-control</update></pen>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="applied" color="-10899396" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot applied-control</update></pen>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="passive" color="-13345367" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot passive-term</update></pen>
      <pen interval="1.0" mode="0" display="load" color="-16777216" legend="true"><setup></setup><update>plot external-load</update></pen>
    </plot>
  </widgets>
  <info><![CDATA[## PURPOSE

Experiment 003 is a minimal contrast between passive relaxation and bounded proportional negative feedback. It asks whether measurements can distinguish return caused by ambient physics from active regulation.

This model intentionally uses only standard NetLogo controls, monitors, patches, markers, and plots. It is not a generic controller framework.

## DYNAMICS

Each deterministic tick applies:

`temperature(t+1) = temperature + passive term + applied control + external load`

The passive term is `relaxation rate * (ambient - temperature)`. In the feedback arm, commanded control is the bounded value of `-controller gain * (sensed temperature - setpoint)`. The passive arm commands zero. Disabling the actuator sets applied control to zero without hiding the command.

Blocking the sensor pins its reported value to the setpoint, as declared by the frozen-sensor preregistration. A persistent load contributes the selected amount on every later tick.

## USE

1. Choose passive or feedback, set parameters, and press Setup.
2. Press Step or Go.
3. Displace the state, apply a persistent load, block the sensor, or disable the actuator.
4. Compare actual temperature, sensed temperature, target, and the four additive dynamics terms.
5. Export the complete flat trajectory when needed.

## EVIDENCE BOUNDARY

The embedded BehaviorSpace experiments specify paired displacement and persistent-load arms plus feedback runs with a blocked sensor or disabled actuator. They are preregistration instruments only at this stage; their results must be run and interpreted separately.]]></info>
